{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: AC machines on the mains",
  "exampleId": "block-ac-machines",
  "description": "Each machine has two pole pairs, so its synchronous speed at 50 Hz is 2π · 50 / 2 = 157.1 rad/s. The induction machine accelerates until its slip is almost zero. The permanent-magnet and reluctance machines start as induction machines on their damper cages and then pull into step, running at exactly synchronous speed. The permanent-magnet machine is fed at its rated 112.3 V rms, which matches its magnet voltage; well below it, the magnets brake the start and it keeps slipping poles.",
  "duration": 3,
  "revision": 0,
  "blocks": [
